        "original_id": "45114962-99b4-509d-ae1d-8478c25ee7ce",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: André Previn, Edie Landau, Eugene O'Neill, Boris Kaufman, Ely A. Landau\n- Works: Long Day's Journey into Night (1962 film), O'Neill's play, The Pawnbroker, The Chosen, The American Film Theatre\n- Roles: composer, pianist, conductor, film producer, TV producer, executive, cinematographer\n\nFacts:\n- André George Previn was born Andreas Ludwig Priwin on April 6, 1929, and he became a German-American pianist, conductor, and composer.\n- Edie Landau was born Edythe Rudolph on July 15, 1927, and she became an American film and TV producer and executive.\n- The 1962 film Long Day's Journey into Night used Eugene O'Neill's play directly rather than adapting the screenplay.\n- André Previn composed the music score for the 1962 film Long Day's Journey into Night.\n- Boris Kaufman was the cinematographer for the 1962 film Long Day's Journey into Night.\n- Edie Landau was known for films including Long Day's Journey into Night, The Pawnbroker, and The Chosen.\n- Edie Landau produced the fourteen films of The American Film Theatre with her husband Ely A. Landau.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
